WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.416 --> 00:00:03.744
- Everyday we have new
issues, new problems,

00:00:03.744 --> 00:00:05.371
new challenges.

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:08.221
I am the first among the equals

00:00:08.221 --> 00:00:10.519
as far as the mentoring
process is concerned.

00:00:10.519 --> 00:00:13.040
I have learned that courage

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.445
is the most important
attribute of a great leader.

00:00:17.445 --> 00:00:20.713
Never ever under estimate
your competitors.

00:00:20.713 --> 00:00:21.936
Half of the people in the country

00:00:21.936 --> 00:00:23.280
are waiting for a telephone,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.736
the other half are
waiting for a dial tone.

00:00:25.736 --> 00:00:26.744
I think at the end of the day

00:00:26.744 --> 00:00:28.109
most of our energy

00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:30.125
comes from mental energy.

00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:32.941
People see us walking the talk.

00:00:32.941 --> 00:00:36.892
Luck you need, but be
prepared to seize that luck.

00:00:36.892 --> 00:00:39.871
Let the good news take the stairs,

00:00:39.871 --> 00:00:43.287
and let the bad news take the elevator.

00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:45.727
While we take our work very seriously,

00:00:45.727 --> 00:00:48.232
we don't take ourselves very seriously.

00:00:48.232 --> 00:00:51.094
- He's an Indian IT industrialist.

00:00:51.094 --> 00:00:52.632
He's the co-founder of Infosys,

00:00:52.632 --> 00:00:55.708
a multi-national corporation
providing business consulting,

00:00:55.708 --> 00:00:58.630
engineering, and outsourcing services.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:00.192
As of September 2015,

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:01.957
he was listed by Forbes magazine

00:01:01.957 --> 00:01:05.699
as having a net worth
of 1.8 billion dollars.

00:01:05.699 --> 00:01:07.622
He's N. R. Narayana Murthy

00:01:07.622 --> 00:01:11.205
and here are his top
ten rules for success.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:16.773
- Everyday we have new
issues, new problems,

00:01:16.773 --> 00:01:18.225
new challenges.

00:01:18.225 --> 00:01:20.169
There is no doubt at all.

00:01:20.169 --> 00:01:23.252
In fact I would always say that today

00:01:24.494 --> 00:01:28.491
it's the nimble ones
that eat the big ones,

00:01:28.491 --> 00:01:29.324
right?

00:01:29.324 --> 00:01:31.732
It's not, size has value,

00:01:31.732 --> 00:01:35.335
but not as much value as it
used to have 50 years ago,

00:01:35.335 --> 00:01:36.812
or 30 years ago.

00:01:36.812 --> 00:01:38.979
So in that sense certainly

00:01:40.511 --> 00:01:44.779
those corporations which
use speed, imagination,

00:01:44.779 --> 00:01:46.686
and excellence and execution

00:01:46.686 --> 00:01:49.772
are the ones that will
survive and succeed.

00:01:49.772 --> 00:01:52.013
So it is absolutely necessary

00:01:52.013 --> 00:01:56.229
for us to come up with
new ideas, new paradigms,

00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:59.259
it is necessary for us to
keep our employees happy,

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:01.804
our customers happy, our investors happy.

00:02:01.804 --> 00:02:04.637
So I don't think the ride is easy.

00:02:05.485 --> 00:02:10.232
- On a scale of one to ten how
would you say you're fairing?

00:02:10.232 --> 00:02:13.111
- I would probably say a six.

00:02:13.111 --> 00:02:15.164
- So that leaves some
pretty significant headroom.

00:02:15.164 --> 00:02:16.761
- Oh yeah, of course, of course.

00:02:16.761 --> 00:02:18.639
But remember that we Infosyians

00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:21.722
are not used to giving high marks so.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.582
The primary objective of every leader

00:02:26.582 --> 00:02:28.298
is to ensure that there is

00:02:28.298 --> 00:02:30.248
successive generation of leaders.

00:02:30.248 --> 00:02:34.143
And one of the instruments for doing that

00:02:34.143 --> 00:02:35.863
is mentoring.

00:02:35.863 --> 00:02:38.606
Mentoring is a private relationship.

00:02:38.606 --> 00:02:40.814
It's a voluntary relationship.

00:02:40.814 --> 00:02:43.461
The mentee chooses the mentor at Infosys,

00:02:43.461 --> 00:02:45.336
so it's an honest one.

00:02:45.336 --> 00:02:46.503
It's one where

00:02:48.111 --> 00:02:49.577
the model dilemna,

00:02:49.577 --> 00:02:52.662
the value system, etc., etc.,

00:02:52.662 --> 00:02:54.990
can be discussed openly and honestly.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:57.798
And hopefully the mentor
will use his or her

00:02:57.798 --> 00:03:02.026
experiential base to give some solutions.

00:03:02.026 --> 00:03:04.515
- So do you have mentoring
throughout the company,

00:03:04.515 --> 00:03:07.855
normally established and you are chief?

00:03:07.855 --> 00:03:10.232
You're chief people officer?

00:03:10.232 --> 00:03:12.836
- I am the first among the equals

00:03:12.836 --> 00:03:15.595
as far as the mentoring
process is concerned.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:19.588
I have learned that courage
is the most important

00:03:19.588 --> 00:03:21.921
attribute of a great leader.

00:03:23.345 --> 00:03:25.302
Courage to dream big,

00:03:25.302 --> 00:03:27.146
courage of conviction,

00:03:27.146 --> 00:03:29.884
courage to take bold decisions,

00:03:29.884 --> 00:03:32.916
courage to go against conventional wisdom,

00:03:32.916 --> 00:03:36.666
and courage to travel
the road less traveled.

00:03:37.758 --> 00:03:41.433
We have learned a lot from
every one of our competitors.

00:03:41.433 --> 00:03:43.780
That is not it at all and we respect them.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:47.659
One of the articles of faith at Infosys is

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:51.119
never ever underestimate your competitors.

00:03:51.119 --> 00:03:53.484
Always respect them.

00:03:53.484 --> 00:03:55.521
Learn what you can from them.

00:03:55.521 --> 00:03:57.971
And that's the way you can beat them.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:01.798
There was a huge opportunity for software

00:04:01.798 --> 00:04:03.644
to be developed for corporations

00:04:03.644 --> 00:04:05.405
because hardware had become cheaper

00:04:05.405 --> 00:04:08.755
and we realized that in India
there were lots of engineers

00:04:08.755 --> 00:04:10.820
who did not have job opportunities.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.293
Therefore we said,

00:04:12.293 --> 00:04:17.015
"Why don't we build a company
that focuses on developing

00:04:17.015 --> 00:04:19.515
"bespoke software applications

00:04:21.006 --> 00:04:23.496
"for customers in developed nations."

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.968
- You started the company
and you had a hard time

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:30.174
because India was not open
to the outside world was it?

00:04:30.174 --> 00:04:31.257
- Those days,

00:04:32.614 --> 00:04:36.281
the government was very
business unfriendly.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.332
It took us a year to get
a telephone connection.

00:04:42.332 --> 00:04:45.406
We used to have a joke and that is

00:04:45.406 --> 00:04:48.300
half the people in the country
are waiting for a telephone,

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.286
the other half are
waiting for a dial tone.

00:04:52.286 --> 00:04:56.266
And second, it took us
three years to get a license

00:04:56.266 --> 00:04:58.594
to import a computer.

00:04:58.594 --> 00:04:59.744
- And that was what you were about.

00:04:59.744 --> 00:05:02.295
You needed a computer to
do the job you were doing.

00:05:02.295 --> 00:05:03.547
- Absolutely

00:05:03.547 --> 00:05:07.926
So the environment was
extremely business unfriendly.

00:05:07.926 --> 00:05:10.139
But then we said,

00:05:10.139 --> 00:05:13.220
"Look there is a huge global opportunity

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:15.046
"and therefore we should stick with it."

00:05:15.046 --> 00:05:18.460
We stuck with it and
God has been kind to us.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.878
I think at the end of the day,

00:05:19.878 --> 00:05:23.633
most of our energy comes
from mental energy.

00:05:23.633 --> 00:05:26.716
As long as you are in a state of mind

00:05:28.207 --> 00:05:31.562
that is full of enthusiasm, hope,

00:05:31.562 --> 00:05:33.401
confidence, and joy,

00:05:33.401 --> 00:05:35.512
then physical energy will come.

00:05:35.512 --> 00:05:39.040
You know frankly I don't think we dreamed

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.666
that we would come this far.

00:05:40.666 --> 00:05:44.455
I don't think we dreamed that
we would be 92,000 people.

00:05:44.455 --> 00:05:48.837
Would probably have 10
or 12 million square feet

00:05:48.837 --> 00:05:49.995
of space.

00:05:49.995 --> 00:05:50.993
I don't think we dreamed

00:05:50.993 --> 00:05:53.579
there'd be four million
dollars plus in revenue.

00:05:53.579 --> 00:05:55.935
A billion dollars plus in profits

00:05:55.935 --> 00:05:58.418
and on 20 million dollars in market gap.

00:05:58.418 --> 00:06:00.935
Operating in 39 countries.

00:06:00.935 --> 00:06:03.637
None of that was dreamed.

00:06:03.637 --> 00:06:06.266
I think what was very clear in our mind

00:06:06.266 --> 00:06:07.525
right from day one

00:06:07.525 --> 00:06:10.512
was that we would seek respect.

00:06:10.512 --> 00:06:13.492
Respect from every one
of our stake holders,

00:06:13.492 --> 00:06:17.427
customers, employees,
investors, rendor partners,

00:06:17.427 --> 00:06:18.989
government of the land and the society.

00:06:18.989 --> 00:06:21.730
Because our logic was if we sought respect

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.543
from every one of these stake holders,

00:06:24.543 --> 00:06:26.923
the revenues would automatically come.

00:06:26.923 --> 00:06:28.558
Profits would come, etc., etc.

00:06:28.558 --> 00:06:30.727
- You know that's the part, to be honest,

00:06:30.727 --> 00:06:31.780
that I don't understand.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:36.488
When you say that you sought
respect from all stake holders

00:06:36.488 --> 00:06:39.163
and everything else would follow.

00:06:39.163 --> 00:06:41.635
How do you actually
hold that in your hand?

00:06:41.635 --> 00:06:44.601
How do you grasp at something tangible

00:06:44.601 --> 00:06:46.452
like respect from stake holders?

00:06:46.452 --> 00:06:48.290
How do you break it down into a process

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:51.654
so that all of Infosys
can identify with it?

00:06:51.654 --> 00:06:52.654
- Well it is

00:06:54.504 --> 00:06:55.412
not that difficult

00:06:55.412 --> 00:06:58.329
in the sense that you articulate a,

00:07:00.496 --> 00:07:01.529
your value system

00:07:01.529 --> 00:07:04.887
in a very clear and concise manner.

00:07:04.887 --> 00:07:09.054
For example we use the acronym
CLIFE for our value system.

00:07:10.136 --> 00:07:12.175
That is C-L-I-F-E.

00:07:12.175 --> 00:07:14.175
Customer focused, Leadership by example,

00:07:14.175 --> 00:07:16.980
Integrity and transparency, Fairness,

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:18.984
and Excellence in execution.

00:07:18.984 --> 00:07:21.812
So we have clear, solid case studies

00:07:21.812 --> 00:07:25.493
all to demonstrate the value system.

00:07:25.493 --> 00:07:28.179
We have leaders talking about it.

00:07:28.179 --> 00:07:30.012
And then people see us

00:07:31.179 --> 00:07:33.304
walking the talk.

00:07:33.304 --> 00:07:37.153
And there are situations where
you could take a short-cut

00:07:37.153 --> 00:07:39.031
and we don't do that.

00:07:39.031 --> 00:07:41.739
And once you demonstrate

00:07:41.739 --> 00:07:43.822
the value system by deed,

00:07:45.026 --> 00:07:46.526
then the grapevine

00:07:48.242 --> 00:07:49.752
travels so fast--

00:07:49.752 --> 00:07:50.782
- And it replicates itself

00:07:50.782 --> 00:07:52.503
- Yeah, it replicates itself.

00:07:52.503 --> 00:07:56.502
You need luck because I've
seen lots of smart people

00:07:56.502 --> 00:07:59.502
lots of people who have worked hard.

00:08:00.512 --> 00:08:02.679
They haven't been blessed.

00:08:04.418 --> 00:08:06.720
And you need luck but at the same time

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:10.182
let's remember Louis Pasteur's words

00:08:10.182 --> 00:08:13.688
that God favors the prepared mind.

00:08:13.688 --> 00:08:17.572
So you have to be prepared to
take advantage of that luck.

00:08:17.572 --> 00:08:22.140
Luck you need, but be
prepared to seize that luck.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.623
I have learned

00:08:23.623 --> 00:08:28.338
that the leaders will have
to be trustworthy first,

00:08:28.338 --> 00:08:31.417
before being high performers.

00:08:31.417 --> 00:08:33.084
Such trustworthiness

00:08:34.267 --> 00:08:37.929
comes if we act according to the adages.

00:08:37.929 --> 00:08:41.354
Let the good news take the stairs

00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:44.930
and let the bad news take the elevator.

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:45.763
- Does it bother you

00:08:45.763 --> 00:08:47.899
that expectations always run so high

00:08:47.899 --> 00:08:49.532
of Nayarana Muthy of Infosys?

00:08:49.532 --> 00:08:52.943
And you know with the expectations
always running so high

00:08:52.943 --> 00:08:54.069
and so consistently high

00:08:54.069 --> 00:08:56.990
there's a risk of people
around you expecting too much

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:59.504
and hence, facing disappointment.

00:08:59.504 --> 00:09:00.962
Does that bother you at all?

00:09:00.962 --> 00:09:02.495
- Not really because,

00:09:02.495 --> 00:09:05.041
while we take our work very seriously,

00:09:05.041 --> 00:09:07.700
we don't take ourselves very seriously.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:12.483
All these things would
bother a person if he or she

00:09:12.483 --> 00:09:15.260
were to take himself or
herself very seriously.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:16.729
We don't do that.

00:09:16.729 --> 00:09:18.900
- And how does a corporation manage

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:20.941
to not take itself so seriously?

00:09:20.941 --> 00:09:23.250
- No the corporation takes it seriously,

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.439
but not the individuals.

00:09:24.439 --> 00:09:26.673
- Not the individuals
within the corporation.

00:09:26.673 --> 00:09:27.858
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:27.858 --> 00:09:31.276
I'm made this video because
Jiashu Chen asked me to.

00:09:31.276 --> 00:09:32.599
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:09:32.599 --> 00:09:34.233
that you want me to profile next,

00:09:34.233 --> 00:09:36.430
leave it in the comments below
and I'll see what I can do.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.931
I'd also love to know
which of the top ten rules

00:09:38.931 --> 00:09:41.123
meant the most to you,
hit you the hardest.

00:09:41.123 --> 00:09:43.770
Leave it in the comments and
I'll join in the discusion.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.134
Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:45.134 --> 00:09:48.717
Continue to believe,
and I'll see you soon.

